To configure the STM32G474 at **170 MHz** with a fixed **3.6 V** supply, the device must operate in **Voltage Scaling Range 1 Boost Mode** (`VOS = 0b01` in `PWR_CR1` and `R1MODE = 0` in `PWR_CR5`) [STM32G474_RM0440 p. 232–233].

### 1. Requirements & Parameters
* **Target System Frequency ($SYSCLK$):** $170\text{ MHz}$ [STM32G474_Datasheet p. 84, 123].
* **Flash Latency:** 4 wait states (`LATENCY = 4` in `FLASH_ACR`) [STM32G474_RM0440 p. 98].
* **PLL VCO Output Range:** $96\text{--}344\text{ MHz}$ in Range 1 Boost mode [STM32G474_Datasheet p. 123].

---

### 2. RCC & Power Configuration Code

```c
#include "stm32g4xx.h"

void SystemClock_Config_170MHz(void)
{
    // 1. Enable Power interface clock
    RCC->APB1ENR1 |= RCC_APB1ENR1_PWREN;

    // 2. Configure Voltage Scaling Range 1 Boost Mode
    // VOS = 0b01 (Range 1) in PWR_CR1
    PWR->CR1 &= ~PWR_CR1_VOS;
    PWR->CR1 |= (1UL << PWR_CR1_VOS_Pos);

    // Clear R1MODE in PWR_CR5 for Boost mode (> 150 MHz up to 170 MHz)
    PWR->CR5 &= ~PWR_CR5_R1MODE;

    // Wait until VOSF flag is cleared in PWR_SR2
    while ((PWR->SR2 & PWR_SR2_VOSF) != 0);

    // 3. Configure Flash Wait States (4 WS for 170 MHz)
    FLASH->ACR &= ~FLASH_ACR_LATENCY;
    FLASH->ACR |= FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_4WS;

    // Enable Instruction cache, Data cache, and Prefetch
    FLASH->ACR |= FLASH_ACR_ICEN | FLASH_ACR_DCEN | FLASH_ACR_PRFTEN;

    // 4. Configure HSI and PLL
    RCC->CR |= RCC_CR_HSION;
    while((RCC->CR & RCC_CR_HSIRDY) == 0);

    // Disable PLL before reconfiguration
    RCC->CR &= ~RCC_CR_PLLON;
    while((RCC->CR & RCC_CR_PLLRDY) != 0);

    // Set PLL Source to HSI, M, N, R dividers
    RCC->PLLCFGR = (2UL << RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLSRC_Pos) |  // PLL source = HSI
                   ((4UL - 1UL) << RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLM_Pos) | // PLLM = 4
                   (85UL << RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLN_Pos) |    // PLLN = 85
                   (0UL << RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLR_Pos) |     // PLLR = 2 (0b00)
                   RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLREN;                 // Enable PLL R output

    // Enable PLL and wait for ready
    RCC->CR |= RCC_CR_PLLON;
    while((RCC->CR & RCC_CR_PLLRDY) == 0);

    // 5. Select PLL as System Clock Source
    RCC->CFGR &= ~RCC_CFGR_SW;
    RCC->CFGR |= RCC_CFGR_SW_PLL;

    // Wait until PLL is selected as system clock
    while ((RCC->CFGR & RCC_CFGR_SWS) != RCC_CFGR_SWS_PLL);
}
```

